, "tests/test_dezoomify_argv.py", "tests/test_repo_hygiene.py", "tvart.py", "urls_to_json.py", "uv.lock"], "files_oracle": [".claude/rules/learnings/tooling.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/boundary-patterns.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-wave-5-split.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/observability-strategy.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/player-contract.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/project-preferences.md"], "findings": [], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 0, "note": 0}, "observations": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "Six blank lines left in tests/test_repo_hygiene.py where the loader-unit tests were cut; black --check at the root will fail", "recommendation": "Between `_directives_of` and the first `@pytest.mark.parametrize` (staged lines 118-123) there are six consecutive blank lines. The root is not excluded from black (`extend-exclude` covers only the three projects), and the CI root job's 'The governance suite' step runs `uv run black --check .`, which normalises top-level gaps to two and so fails. The recorded test evidence covers pytest only, so a green suite says nothing about this. Run `uv run black .` at the root before committing. Scope: instance, left over from deleting two functions and their constants by hand.", "files": ["tests/test_repo_hygiene.py"], "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "tv_api_check lets ConfigError escape as a traceback when the Player has no Frame output or an incomplete .env", "recommendation": "`_frame()` raises `ConfigError` with a clear message, which `test_the_api_check_refuses_a_client_with_no_television` pins. But the first call comes from `run()`'s opening `print`, and neither `run()` nor `main()` catches it, so an operator gets a stack trace instead of the one-line refusal the docstring promises. The 2024 `config.py` failed the same way at import, so nothing got worse. Even so, catching `ConfigError` in `main()` (print the message, return 2, matching the missing-image path) and testing it through `main()` would complete the refusal. Scope: instance.", "files": ["arrt-player/tools/tv_api_check.py", "arrt-player/tests/test_tools.py"], "oid": "O-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "feed_guard.problems now skips semantic_errors on a schema-invalid document, and no test covers that branch", "recommendation": "The change is sound: every caller asserts `problems(...) == []`, so no assertion got weaker, and `semantic_errors` now states its precondition. But the new branch (schema errors returned, semantic rules not consulted, no KeyError) is never exercised; every caller passes a valid feed. One case that feeds `problems()` a document missing `works` and asserts it returns schema messages without raising would pin the reason the docstring gives. Scope: instance.", "files": ["arrt/tests/feed_guard.py"], "oid": "O-3"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "Live-unit test docstring still points at the deleted loader unit and config.py", "recommendation": "`test_a_live_unit_declares_its_environment_file` opens 'Same requirement as the loader unit' and explains it by '`config.py` raises at import', and both of those were removed in this change. The assertions are right; only the prose is stale, and nothing reads it. Make the explanation relational (the plane's settings refuse to start without their REQUIRED values) or delete the sentence. NOTE-weight, so no fix commit is wanted for this alone. Scope: instance.", "files": ["tests/test_repo_hygiene.py"], "oid": "O-4"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "tv_delete.py now duplicates the Player's own confirmed removal and UPLOADED_CATEGORY inside the same project", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. Moving `tv_delete.py` into arrt-player put a second confirmed-delete (`delete_list_confirmed`/`DeleteResult`/`DeleteNotConfirmed`) beside `arrt_player.tv.samsung.SamsungTv.remove` (`RemovalOutcome`/`TvRemovalUnconfirmed`), and a second `UPLOADED_CATEGORY = \"MY-C0002\"` beside `arrt_player.tv.client.UPLOADED_CATEGORY`. The docstrings are near-copies too. The plan's own reason for dropping the root `config.py` (\"reaching the set by other settings than the wall's would check something other than the wall\") applies here as well: `tv_api_check`'s 'confirmed delete' check exercises the tool's private copy, so a regression in the removal the daemon actually ships cannot show up in the one hand-run check that talks to the real set. At minimum, import `UPLOADED_CATEGORY` from `arrt_player.tv`. Then either drive `SamsungTv.remove` from the tool and retire `tv_delete.py` and its tests, or record why the tool deliberately keeps an independent wrapper (for example, to probe the library rather than the Player's client).", "files": ["arrt-player/tools/tv_delete.py", "arrt-player/tools/tv_api_check.py", "arrt-player/tests/test_tv_delete.py"], "oid": "O-5"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "Moved tool tests put tools/ on sys.path at module level, unlike the display suite's existing fixture convention", "recommendation": "Scope: class (every display-suite test that imports from `tools/`). `test_panel_check.py` and `test_tv_delete.py` each run `sys.path.insert(0, .../tools)` at import time. That change to the path is permanent and applies to the whole session. Their siblings `test_tools.py` (both fixtures, including the new `api_check`) and `test_power_probe.py` use `monkeypatch.syspath_prepend(str(TOOLS))` instead, so the display suite now has two mechanisms for the same thing, and one of them makes `tools/` importable from every later test whether or not it asked. Pick one owner: either `pythonpath = [\"tools\"]` in arrt-player's `[tool.pytest.ini_options]`, or a shared conftest fixture. Then delete the per-file inserts and the per-fixture prepends.", "files": ["arrt-player/tests/test_panel_check.py", "arrt-player/tests/test_tv_delete.py", "arrt-player/tests/test_tools.py"], "oid": "O-6"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "title": ".env.example still gives the retired command `python tv_api_check.py` for the panel-size check", "recommendation": "Scope: class. Search for `python tv_api_check.py` and bare `tv_api_check.py` run instructions outside history; expect `.prawduct/artifacts/operational-spec.md:636` as a second member outside this diff. `.env.example` ~line 140 tells the operator to run `python tv_api_check.py` and to 'run it on the Pi'. That file is no longer at the root, and the tool now runs as `cd arrt-player && uv run python tools/tv_api_check.py` against the Player's own `.env`. Copied as written, the command fails with file-not-found. This is an actively misleading instruction, which Goal 4 rates BLOCKING at boundary. Replace it with a pointer to the tool's own usage line (its docstring) rather than another copy of the command.", "files": [".env.example"], "oid": "O-7"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "title": "Stale prose about the deleted loader and config.py in surviving and moved files", "recommendation": "Scope: class. Search the files this change kept or moved for 'loader', 'config.py' and 'journal'. Known members: (1) `tests/test_repo_hygiene.py` `test_a_live_unit_declares_its_environment_file` opens 'Same requirement as the loader unit' and says '`config.py` raises at import', but both the unit and that file are gone. (2) The comment in `arrt-player/tools/tv_delete.py` (~line 110) and the docstring of `arrt-player/tests/test_tv_delete.py::test_the_reason_reaches_the_message_and_not_only_the_chain` justify the cause-in-message rule by 'the journal of an unattended loader', but the only caller is now a hand-run tool that prints the exception. (3) `arrt-player/tools/tv_api_check.py` `check_upload` compares against 'the loader's' window. For each: delete the clause or make it relational (for example, 'the caller's output'). Do not add narration.", "files": ["tests/test_repo_hygiene.py", "arrt-player/tools/tv_delete.py", "arrt-player/tests/test_tv_delete.py", "arrt-player/tools/tv_api_check.py"], "oid": "O-8"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "Removing the loader-unit tests left six consecutive blank lines in test_repo_hygiene.py", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. In the staged `tests/test_repo_hygiene.py`, six blank lines sit between `_directives_of` and the first `@pytest.mark.parametrize`. Black collapses module-level gaps to two, so the root CI leg's `uv run black --check .` should reject this file. Reformat it. Also check whether the recorded lint evidence predates this edit.", "files": ["tests/test_repo_hygiene.py"], "oid": "O-9"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "title": "tv_api_check's 'refused by name' for a Player with no television is an uncaught traceback, unlike its sibling tool", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. `_frame()` raises `ConfigError`, and so does `load()` on any malformed `.env`. `main()` and `run()` catch neither, so the operator gets a stack trace that buries the one sentence that matters. Its sibling `label_preview.py` catches the settings failure and prints `could not read this deployment's settings: ...`. Catch `ConfigError` in `main()`, print its message, and return a non-zero status. The existing `test_the_api_check_refuses_a_client_with_no_television` can then drive `main()` instead of `_frame()`.", "files": ["arrt-player/tools/tv_api_check.py"], "oid": "O-10"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "test_file_organization keeps an always-empty allowlist as a frozenset constant", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. `_ROOT_MODULES` is now `frozenset()`, and its comment says the set can only ever shrink, so `present <= _ROOT_MODULES` is just `not present` dressed as an allowlist. Asserting `present == set()` directly would be simpler and say the rule plainly. The canary `assert present` went with the modules, so this guard now passes if `_tracked()` returns nothing. A replacement canary on `_tracked()` being non-empty would restore it. That part is for the correctness reviewer; it is noted here only because the simplification and the canary sit on the same line.", "files": ["tests/preferences/test_file_organization.py"], "oid": "O-11"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "title": "rule-unenforced: the retirement grep ('When you retire, amend, descope or close anything, first grep the whole repo') has no check, and the 2024 retirement left live survivors in the norm artifact", "recommendation": "Class, not instance. Core learning 'When you retire, amend, descope or close anything, first grep the whole repo (no --include) for its nouns and OLD wording' is written, and chunk 02's own Done-when restates it ('A whole-repo grep (no --include) for each removed filename finds only history'), but nothing runs it: record_lint's `retired-claim-survives` needs a `Retires:` phrase this project's change log never declares, and the manifest shows it counted 0. The sweep that edited project-preferences.md (an oracle file; Records Pass) stopped at the rows it touched. Survivors that currently describe the tree, checked against the staged index: (a) \u00a7 Tooling 'Dev commands': `python tvart.py [--flags]` is the entry point for the 2024 modules, a command for a deleted file (Records Pass bar 3, a wrong command; BLOCKING at boundary). (b) the '`requirements.txt` vs `deploy/pi-freeze-2024.txt`' bullet, which says requirements.txt 'is ... the set installed on the Pi' and that omni_epd/IT8951 'are declared in requirements.txt now'. (c) \u00a7 Key libraries: omni-epd 'Declared in requirements.txt'; '`openai` (`ai.py`) ... Real per-call spend'; dezoomify-rs 'Not configured in config.py ... literals in image_utils.py'. (d) \u00a7 Type annotations and \u00a7 Error handling / \u00a7 Async, which state current state in terms of config.py, ai.py, art.py, display.py, tvart.py and others. (e) norm-index rows: the broad-except row's Enforcement column still reads 'the root's four 2024 modules carved out until the legacy retirement' (the root pyproject now has no BLE001 carve-out), so it overclaims a waiver; the ANN row