mong the files to move. An owner scanning the dispositions, which is where applicability is recorded, would read no departure. Fix: re-dispose that line as `exception` (or `ruling needed`), pointing at the mid-build decision, and give the decision the plan's own `[DECISION: ... | user can veto]` form, so the owner rules on it before the boundary review instead of discovering it there. The reasoning itself is sound: config.py required ART_ROOT, LATITUDE, LONGITUDE and LOCATION_NAME at import, which a Player does not set.", "files": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-wave-5-split.md"], "oid": "O-13"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "title": "Mid-build decisions for the owner (Goal 5 roll-up)", "recommendation": "Scope: none. What the plan records as decided mid-build, and what settled each. Chunk 01: (1) the data stays at contract/schemas and the other data paths, carried by force-include ('do it right', because 58 files cite the paths); (2) player-contract.md ships through a symlink (the wave 5 row); (3) the Player's suite does not import semantic_errors (an error in the plan, corrected, not settled by the goals); (4) the package's tests are three moved root files plus test_package.py; (5) post-review fixes carried into 02 (the core learnings rule on cheap observations). Chunk 02: (6) the tools read arrt_player.config rather than carrying config.py, a departure from an owner ruling (see the separate observation); (7) all.json and pi-freeze-2024.txt stay, because the plan's list was wrong about both; (8) remove_from_tv, forgettable_ids and describe_removal left with tvart.py, along with ten tests, and two message tests were rewritten against delete_list_confirmed; (9) tests/test_config.py was split into tests/preferences/test_deployment_values.py, with the 2024 config and unit tests leaving with their subjects; (10) the 2024 sections of deploy/README.md were removed. One new direct dependency, requests>=2.32 in arrt-player/pyproject.toml, carries its reason inline. The goals' four owner answers are all ruled, and the six open assumptions are labelled [MED|LOW impact | user can override].", "files": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-wave-5-split.md", "arrt-player/pyproject.toml"], "oid": "O-14"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "title": "tv_api_check.py: a missing Player setting surfaces as an asyncio traceback, not a refusal by name with an exit code", "recommendation": "Instance. `_frame()` raises `ConfigError` when there is no Frame output, and `load()` raises it for any missing REQUIRED value. Either one is first reached inside `run()`, at the opening print, under `asyncio.run`, so the operator gets a full traceback. The tool's other pre-flight refusal (a missing `--image`) prints one line and returns 2. The failure is detectable, since the message names the variable, so nothing is silent. Making it consistent is a single `except ConfigError` in `main()` that prints the message and returns 2. NOTE weight.", "files": ["arrt-player/tools/tv_api_check.py"], "oid": "O-15"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "title": "Backlog item appears resolved: brookstalley/arrt#33 'tooling: give the broad-except norm a linter half via BLE001 + noqa'", "recommendation": "Scope: none. Since 2026-10-05, BLE has been selected in every plane's ruff config. This change removes the root's last BLE001 per-file carve-outs (image_utils.py, metadata.py, source_utils.py, tvart.py) along with the modules, so the root now runs BLE with no exemption. Verify it, then call `/prawduct:backlog update 33 status=shipped closed-by=scope:wave-5-split` when the backlog skill's 'When to mark shipped' rule says. Reconciliation was run from the cache (brookstalley/arrt, confirmed 1h old) with `affecting` over the removed and moved paths, plus `search` on the legacy nouns. Every legacy-tv item it found (#19, #32, #52, #56, #73) and #4, #5, #6, #31 and #43 are already closed. The open items #41, #65, #70, #109, #107, #166 and #263 are not resolved by this change.", "files": ["pyproject.toml"], "oid": "O-16"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "title": "Learnings cross-check and Records Pass coverage", "recommendation": "Scope: none. Learnings read via `learnings-files --for-diff`: core.md, display.md, tooling.md. One regression against a rule, the retirement grep, is folded into the rule-unenforced observation above. The only rule-file change this cycle is tooling.md's new `contract/pyproject.toml` path glob, which is correctly placed and is not a duplicate. Records Pass covered all six oracle files: tooling.md, boundary-patterns.md, build-plan-wave-5-split.md, observability-strategy.md, player-contract.md and project-preferences.md. Only project-preferences.md cleared a bar (above). The plan's governed_by paperwork is the separate Goal 5 observation. The boundary-patterns, observability-strategy and player-contract edits match the staged tree. Priors: none (prior_dispositions empty).", "files": [".prawduct/artifacts/project-preferences.md"], "oid": "O-17"}], "duration_seconds": 540, "scope": "wave-5-split", "scope_chosen_by": "binding", "scope_unresolved_cause": null, "scope_reason": null, "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": [], "chunks_proposed": [], "chunk": null, "base_reviewed": null, "record_lint": {"records": [".claude/rules/learnings/tooling.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/boundary-patterns.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-wave-5-split.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/observability-strategy.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/player-contract.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/project-preferences.md", "CLAUDE.md", "README.md", "deploy/README.md"], "chunk_graded": "01", "chunks_graded": ["01"], "plan_graded": ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-wave-5-split.md", "findings": [], "unchecked": ["chunk-ref-missing graded chunk 01 of .prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-wave-5-split.md: chunk 01 was inferred as the plan's first open chunk (`plan_status.current_chunks`) because the dispatch carried no chunk \u2014 a chunk whose review is not y